[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged by subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject))
and marked known: one issue, one fix queued. Placed by tenant and channel, its reports are two
problems. The queued parser fix closes only one of them.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one issue. Each problem below has its own cause and needs its own ticket and fix.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

Counted the desk's way, with the desk's own view as exported on 4 October: one report per id (the
export lists some reports twice), placed by tenant and channel, not by subject or intake tag.

## The problems

### `parser`: dates read month first

Ticket: **#1**. The shared parser reads every date month first. Our tenants all write the day first,
so a booking for 7 April comes out as 4 July. It reaches every tenant, through the app, by email and
through the booking-v2 form. This is the bug #4471 was opened for, and the fix that is queued.

The reports the desk read as a one-day move are filed here by tenant and counted here, as the footnote
under the table says. Their bodies show no day/month swap ("Tuesday 6 October showed as Monday", the same
meeting on different days in Lisbon and Toronto). Check them again once the parser fix ships.

### `hint`: booking-v3 asks for the month first

Ticket: **#2**. booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. On a day-first tenant, people type
the month first as the hint tells them, and the form reads the date the tenant's way, day first. The
date comes out flipped, but the parser fix does not touch it: once the parser reads day first, these
reports keep coming. Only the form reaches them, on booking-v3 tenants.

## How to read a report

- Place a report by its tenant's locale and booking form, not by its subject.
  The same subjects come in for both problems above.
- Do not use the intake tag. It follows the reporter's browser, not the cause.

